ple all the time and  say hey you're wrong you're a [ __ ]  you're an idiot you're a fraud you're a  scam that's not how the world works at  some point what we have to realize is  that rather than be abrasive the best  path sometimes is to listen  to hear what somebody is saying and to  simply say you know what here is where  the common ground is we both agree that  bitcoin is the greatest store of value  in the market amazing by the way you  think that there's a low probability  that it could become a medium of  exchange well other people think that  there's a high probability and therefore  let us explain to you why  and then allow him to say i agree or i  disagree and here's why and have a  conversation about it now i fully think  that there's plenty of other people like  this that are going to come into the  market that are going to have opinions  some of them actually are going to be  very uneducated right one of the things  that i think the bitcoin community gets  right is that the critics of bitcoin  frankly aren't that intelligent they're  not that well informed and we're lucky  to have such ridiculously  low  uh prepared critics i love the fact that  they show up and they say things that  were being said back in 2012 that have  been disproved for almost a decade great  they sound like idiots  but  mark cuban and there's others they  actually are very well informed and in  many cases they're not actually a critic  what they're trying to do is have a  rational conversation say hey here's  what i believe this is why i own the  asset i actually see great value in it  but here's the challenges i see here's  the obstacles i see moving forward  sometimes those rational conversations  are really worth it right  yeah i listened to the uh the twitter  spaces you were up late past your  bedtime listen yeah  go ahead i put ranger to bed first and  then yeah uh no but i listened to the  conversation and i thought it was  interesting because first off  regardless of what your opinion is on on  his specific uh kind of overview of of  bitcoin or other cryptos or whatever you  have to respect the fact that he came in  the room with 15 000 people that didn't  like him right and we're gonna set to  argue against them and then second off i  think he was on the treadmill or  something which was pretty funny in its  own right uh but so i i certainly  respect the idea that he came in the  room ready to fight right and that's the  other point of it too is right like you  have to expect someone to be a little uh  when everyone's coming at them you have  to expect them to kind of give you a  little heat back and he certainly did  that but at the same time right like  he's made a lot of comments in the past  that he's contradicted himself he said  certain things about bitcoin that not  necessarily everyone agrees with uh so  there's certainly some history there as  to why people don't trust what he has to  say or trust his opinion or or find his  uh opinion to be uh  intelligent on it right i'd say so i  think there there's some concern there  but ultimately you're right in the  aspect of like he did agree on some  things right he said bitcoin's the  biggest the best store of value in the  world he owns he owns it uh he talked  about dogecoin and some other things but  i think ultimately he agrees on a lot of  things the one main point of contention  that he pushed back on was just seeing  uh bitcoin as a medium of exchange right  and saying hey look uh most of the  bitcoiners believe that we'll get to a  point where there's hundreds of billions  if not billions of people globally that  have adopted bitcoin are using it as a  medium of exchange mark doesn't think  that we'll get that right he just says  that there's better technology there's  better uh kind of projects out there  that might get there quicker or have an  advantage in doing it and he he made  some good points some points that people  obviously didn't agree with but  ultimately i 